{"school":{"dbn":"15K088","name":"J.H.S. 088 Peter Rouget","boro":"Brooklyn","district":"15","district_label":"District 15","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":841,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"544 7TH AVENUE, BROOKLYN, NY 11215","phone":"(718)840-1950","website":"www.ms88.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/69157","accessibility":"Fully Accessible","overview":"The mission of M.S. 88 is to develop the core values students need to develop themselves inward and outward. Its three houses, School of Media Arts & Technology (SMART), School for Medical & Health Careers (Medical), and School for Integrated Studies through the Arts (SISTA), provide students with supportive communities and the necessary emotional and academic support so that students can think for themselves, problem solve, and add value to their lives and to the world in which they live. Projects engage students in authentic problems and issues in society and provide them with opportunities to apply knowledge and skills. Projects tap different learning modalities and promote multiple ways of demonstrating understanding. Integrated project work is embedded and students are challenged to present solutions to real-world problems. Blended learning within an integrated curriculum aligns to initiatives such as the Gowanus Conservancy and Lego Robotics. Social emotional learning takes place through our Core Values of Curiosity, Empathy, Resilience, Integrity and Respect, which are integrated throughout the day as well as through our Advisory program. Adult development allows teachers to understand themselves and each other as thinkers and as professionals. It is essential for effective communication and collaboration. To realize its mission, Middle School 88 has partnered with universities and other private and public organizations to offer a balanced academic program, as well as enrichment and 